was over and america had won her independence

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:52.480
alexander hamilton returned to new york city&nbsp;
and finished his legal training in july 1782.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.480 --> 00:05:57.520
he plunged into legal work with the same energy he&nbsp;
put into everything else quickly becoming one of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.520 --> 00:06:02.880
new york's most prominent attorneys he also raised&nbsp;
a large family with his wife eliza eventually the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:09.440
couple would have eight children between 1782 and&nbsp;
1802 but hamilton had turned his eye toward a new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:16.400
passion by then politics in the 1780s the new&nbsp;
nation won by blood shed by men like hamilton&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:21.680
was in crisis the united states was governed by&nbsp;
a document known as the articles of confederation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:26.160
under the articles the federal government was&nbsp;
incredibly weak only being able to act with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:31.920
consent of all 13 states and since the states&nbsp;
never seemed to agree on anything nothing was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:38.000
getting done there was no way to mitigate disputes&nbsp;
between states who at times acted like independent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:43.680
countries onto themselves and if things continued&nbsp;
the way they were then it was just a matter of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:49.120
time before the country tore itself apart hamilton&nbsp;
served in the congress of the confederation and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.120 --> 00:06:54.320
knew exactly how poor it was he joined a growing&nbsp;
chorus of politicians who called for the articles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.320 --> 00:06:59.920
to be replaced in may 1787 hamilton was chosen&nbsp;
as one of three representatives from new york&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.920 --> 00:07:05.040
to the constitutional convention in philadelphia&nbsp;
hamilton's influence at the convention was limited&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.040 --> 00:07:09.840
by the two other new york delegates who belonged&nbsp;
to a faction controlled by new york governor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.840 --> 00:07:15.360
george clinton that was opposed to any reform that&nbsp;
would take power away from his state despite this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:20.960
the other delegates headed by convention president&nbsp;
george washington hammered out a brand new united&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:25.280
states constitution over the course of four&nbsp;
months that created a new federal government&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.280 --> 00:07:30.800
made up of an elected president and a congress&nbsp;
who would make laws that covered all the states&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:35.680
but the new constitution would only go into&nbsp;
effect if nine of the 13 states ratified it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:39.680
in state conventions something that wasn't&nbsp;
guaranteed hamilton wanted to help convince&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:44.400
the american people that the new constitution&nbsp;
was not only necessary but it benefited them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:49.040
then they would put pressure on their legislators&nbsp;
to ratify it hamilton enlisted the help of two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.040 --> 00:07:54.880
other passionate supporters of the constitution&nbsp;
fellow new yorker john jay and virginian james&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.880 --> 00:07:59.040
madison and they would write a series of articles&nbsp;
explaining it to the public written under the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:05.360
pseudonym publius the series of 85 articles was&nbsp;
published in major newspapers between october 1787&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:12.000
and april 1788. the federalist papers as they are&nbsp;
known today explained in painstaking detail all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:17.440
of the flaws of the articles of confederation as&nbsp;
well as an in-depth explanation of each article&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.440 --> 00:08:22.880
of the new constitution including how it benefited&nbsp;
the average american citizen the federalist papers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.880 --> 00:08:26.080
were an immediate sensation being widely&nbsp;
read across the country and eventually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:31.840
published in a two-volume book in 1788 the barrage&nbsp;
of well-written and explained arguments in favor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.840 --> 00:08:36.720
of the constitution overwhelmed any opposition&nbsp;
the people began to clamor for their state&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:42.320
legislatures to adopt the new document on june&nbsp;
21 1788 new hampshire became the ninth state&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.320 --> 00:08:47.040
to ratify the constitution officially putting it&nbsp;
into effect one month later hamilton's home state&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:52.160
of new york finally ratified it rather than risk&nbsp;
being left out of the union of the other states&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.160 --> 00:08:57.280
though the identity of publius was officially&nbsp;
a secret most everyone knew that alexander&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.280 --> 00:09:01.360
hamilton was one of the principal authors of&nbsp;
the federalist papers and he would be closely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.360 --> 00:09:06.560
associated with the strong central government laid&nbsp;
out in the constitution for the rest of his life&nbsp;&nbsp;

